nss_core: let the build pick the default QoS memory pool size

The MP firmware (IPQ5018, 12.2-156 and 12.5-210 alike) answers the
flow-queue memory request of nssfq_codel with a zero size unless the
host hands it a QoS pool at core init; without it every nssfq_codel is
refused with "Firmware reported a zero flow queue size". The HK firmware
on ipq807x does not need the pool. The pool is only configured from the
qos_mem_size module parameter, whose default was a fixed 0, so a board
that needs it had to carry the option in /etc/modules.conf by hand.

Take the default from NSS_QOS_MEM_SIZE_DEFAULT when the build defines
it (the ipq50xx Makefile sets 1 MB) and keep 0 otherwise. The module
parameter still overrides it.

--- a/nss_core.c
+++ b/nss_core.c
@@ -93,7 +93,11 @@
 module_param_array(pn_qlimits, short, NULL, 0);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(pn_qlimits, "Queue limit per queue");
 
-static int qos_mem_size = 0;
+#ifndef NSS_QOS_MEM_SIZE_DEFAULT
+#define NSS_QOS_MEM_SIZE_DEFAULT 0
+#endif
+
+static int qos_mem_size = NSS_QOS_MEM_SIZE_DEFAULT;
 module_param(qos_mem_size, int, S_IRUGO);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(qos_mem_size, "QoS memory size");
 
